From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:10:55 +0000
Subject: Detect system ColPack without --with-colpack

The POSIX rewrite of the library-directory loop in colpack.m4 iterates
over an empty list when --with-colpack is not given, so a ColPack
installed in the default search path was never detected.  Use a
"system" placeholder so the link test runs once with plain -lColPack.

This lets Debian drop --with-colpack=/usr, which added a bogus
-Wl,-rpath,/usr/lib64 (lintian: custom-library-search-path).

Forwarded: not-needed (upstream has replaced autotools with CMake)
---
 autoconf/colpack.m4 | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/autoconf/colpack.m4 b/autoconf/colpack.m4
index e87f23a..a707d83 100644
--- a/autoconf/colpack.m4
+++ b/autoconf/colpack.m4
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ fi
 [
 COLPACK_CFLAGS=""
 COLPACK_LIBS="-lColPack"
-D=""
+D="system"
 ])
 
 AC_LANG_PUSH([C++])
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ CPPFLAGS="$save_CPPFLAGS"
 CXXFLAGS="$save_CXXFLAGS"
 ])
 for COLPACK_LIBDIR in $D; do
-if test -n "$COLPACK_LIBDIR" ; then
+if test "x$COLPACK_LIBDIR" != xsystem ; then
 COLPACK_LIBS="-L$COLPACK_LIBDIR -lColPack -Wl,-rpath,$COLPACK_LIBDIR"
 fi
 if test x$have_colpackheaders = xyes ; then
